# this container's mounts + service, both lanes  (vLLM)
#
# build-spec — per-port runtime declaration, sourced by the shared resolver.
# Baked at /opt/resources/build-spec. See base/resolve/build-spec.example for the
# full contract. SOURCED bash: plain arrays/vars, zero dependencies.

# ── SERVICE (required) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vLLM serves the model named in the config file. $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG is a deliberate
# env knob (a config-file SELECTOR with a smart default — not a raw path the user must
# know); $DROSTE_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS (folded in by PRE_LAUNCH below) is the other. Default =
# the persisted /opt/data copy that templates.yaml seeds (if_missing) from the shipped
# template. User may point it elsewhere.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS OURS, NOT UPSTREAM'S — it is not in vllm/envs.py, and argparse_utils.py
# reads only the `--config` FLAG. So it carries the DROSTE_ prefix like every other
# droste-owned setting, and the OLD `VLLM_CONFIG` spelling is simply gone (no backward
# compatibility is owed; a native VLLM_* spelling would be, this was never one).
# ⚠️ Substring noise — VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT and VLLM_CONFIGURE_LOGGING are real and
# UNRELATED upstream variables. A bare grep for VLLM_CONFIG is untrustworthy.
#
# 🚨 A CONFIG WITH NO MODEL DOES NOT FAIL. This comment used to say vLLM exits with
# "model is required"; it does not. ModelConfig.model defaults to Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B
# (config/model.py:103), `model_tag` is nargs="?", and validate_parsed_serve_args
# never checks — so an unedited box DOWNLOADS AND SERVES Qwen3-0.6B and reads
# HEALTHY. What to do about that is a ruling, not a wiring decision (board N21);
# recorded here so the next reader does not inherit the false version.
# ⭐ THE DEFAULT IS A NAMED CONSTANT because it has TWO users: the `:=` here, and the
# blank guard in PRE_LAUNCH that catches the same setting arriving from the user's file
# AFTER this line has already run. Two spellings of one path is how they drift apart.
VLLM_CONFIG_DEFAULT=/opt/data/vllm_config.yaml
: "${DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG:=$VLLM_CONFIG_DEFAULT}"
export DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG
SERVICE=( vllm serve --config "$DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG" )

# ── HEALTH — probe endpoint for droste-healthcheck.sh ────────────────────────
# vLLM's OpenAI server exposes /health (200 when the engine is ready). Weight
# load + graph work happens before it answers, so the podman
# --health-start-period must cover it.
HEALTH_PATH="/health"
HEALTH_ACCEPT="ok"

# ── ENV_FILE (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Seeded from templates/vllm.env (templates.yaml if_missing). vLLM's SERVE FLAGS
# live in the YAML consumed via --config; this file carries the ~209 runtime
# VLLM_* ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES, which are not expressible as YAML keys — several
# are read before any config is parsed. Two mechanisms, so two files.
#
# ⚠️ It is also the only place $DROSTE_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS and $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG can be set.
# Both were advertised by this box (here and in the generated YAML header) while no
# file existed to hold them, which made the catch-all itself unreachable in the
# lane that serves. server.env cannot stand in: it is read in a subshell whose
# output is discarded except for three keys.
#
# ⭐ ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING AND ALREADY CORRECT: the resolver sources this file
# AFTER the build-spec and BEFORE PRE_LAUNCH, and PRE_LAUNCH re-reads
# $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG when it rebuilds SERVICE — so a user's DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG here
# wins over the default set at the top of this file. Do not move the
# `: "${DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG:=...}"` line into PRE_LAUNCH, and do not hardcode the path
# in the rebuild.
# ▶ OPEN QUESTION, NOT RESOLVED HERE: vllm.env's Reserved section lists
#   DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG among the settings a user must NOT set, while this block says
#   a user's value wins. Both cannot be true. TODAY'S BEHAVIOUR IS "the user's value
#   wins" and this wiring keeps it unchanged; the disagreement is queued for a
#   ruling, not settled by whoever edits next.
#
# ⭐ AND IT IS SOURCED UNDER `set -a`, WHICH IS WHY NATIVE LINES NEED NO WIRING.
# Every `VLLM_FOO=bar` a user uncomments is exported by the resolver itself. Only
# the DROSTE_VLLM_* names below need translating — they are the settings where
# passing the user's word through unprocessed would be wrong or fatal.
ENV_FILE="/opt/data/vllm.env"

# ── OVERLAYS (optional) — <upper>:<lower> ────────────────────────────────────
# Overlay the persisted upper over the WHOLE baked venv (captures bin/ console
# scripts too and avoids pinning a pythonX.Y path) so user pip installs persist
# without shadowing the baked torch/vllm stack. The upper is CACHE class (a pip
# install is re-runnable) → /opt/program-cache, which the installer may empty.
OVERLAYS=(
    "/opt/program-cache/venv:/opt/venv"
)

# ── SURFACES (optional) — <src>:<dest> ───────────────────────────────────────
# No container-specific state surfaces beyond caches/config for vLLM.
SURFACES=()

# ── CACHES (optional) — <src>:<dest> ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Persist the torch-stack compute/kernel caches under /opt/program-cache/compute/ with
# zero env vars ($HOME-relative dests so both lanes resolve correctly). THE compute/
# PREFIX IS LOAD-BEARING: it is what the resolver rewrites to the shared /opt/caches
# store when that volume is bound. Triton default cache is ~/.triton/cache (01-rocm-env-
# for-triton.sh sets no TRITON_CACHE_DIR, so the default holds). MIOpen's miopen-db
# row is its machine-written tuning DB (~/.config/miopen is MIOpen's default userdb
# path) in addition to the ~/.cache/miopen kernel cache. The vllm row is vLLM's own
# compile/artifact cache (~/.cache/vllm) — it consciously joins the shared
# /opt/caches store under the v0.2.0 cache policy (owner decision 2026-07-09).
CACHES=(
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen:$HOME/.cache/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/miopen-db:$HOME/.config/miopen"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/triton:$HOME/.triton/cache"
    "/opt/program-cache/compute/vllm:$HOME/.cache/vllm"
)

# ── CRITICAL (optional) — <label>:<path> ─────────────────────────────────────
# HF cache is CRITICAL: unbound => vLLM silently re-downloads multi-GB weights into an
# anonymous volume that vanishes on recreate. Hard-error unless ALLOW_EPHEMERAL.
CRITICAL=(
    "hf-cache:$HOME/.cache/huggingface"
)

# ── OPTIONAL (optional) — <label>:<path>[:<marker>] ──────────────────────────
# A directory of local weights the user may bind; tell-once, don't nag. vLLM can serve a
# model by absolute path (model: /opt/models/...) in the config. Marker body:
# templates/mount_shared_models_here.
OPTIONAL=(
    "models:/opt/models:/opt/models/mount_shared_models_here"
)

# ── The vllm.env → environment table ─────────────────────────────────────────
# vllm.env offers yes/no (or a short menu); vLLM reads its own variables from the
# environment. This table is the translation, and it is the ONLY mapping — adding a
# setting means editing vllm.env AND this file.
#
# 🚨 THERE IS NO SINGLE WIRE VALUE THAT WORKS FOR ALL OF THEM, which is the whole
# reason these are droste-owned rather than passed through. vLLM's own env table
# uses SIX incompatible boolean readers, measured at the pin (vllm/envs.py, v0.16.0):
#
#   bool(int(x))                  "1" only — "true" raises ValueError, server dies
#   .lower() in ("true","1")       either
#   .lower() == "true"             "true" ONLY — "1" reads as False
#   == "1"                         "1" ONLY — "true" reads as False
#   .strip().lower() in ('1','true')  either, and it strips surrounding space
#   is_true() (huggingface_hub's)  upper-cases, matches {1,ON,YES,TRUE}
#
# So the true/false spelling is PER VARIABLE. A user writing `yes` would hit a
# ValueError on the bool(int) rows and a silent False on several others; that is
# exactly the fall-through we do not make users carry.
#
# "<SUFFIX>:<native var>:<ON wire>:<OFF wire>" — ours is DROSTE_VLLM_<SUFFIX>.
#
# ⚠️ THE COLUMNS ARE "WHAT WE WRITE WHEN THE USER SAYS ON/OFF", NOT "TRUE/FALSE".
# Five rows are marked INVERTED: upstream spells the setting as a DISABLE/SKIP, so
# the user's `on` writes a 0. That is not a typo and swapping it back silently
# inverts a working box. Each one names the upstream variable it flips.
VLLM_BOOL_VARS=(
    # ── Model sources ──
    # huggingface_hub's is_true(), not vLLM's: {"1","ON","YES","TRUE"} upper-cased
    "HF_HUB_OFFLINE:HF_HUB_OFFLINE:1:0"
    # .lower() == "true" — "1" would read as FALSE here
    "USE_MODELSCOPE:VLLM_USE_MODELSCOPE:true:false"
    # ── LoRA adapters ── .strip().lower() in ('1','true')
    "RT_LORA_UPDATES_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_RUNTIME_LORA_UPDATING:1:0"
    # ── Caches & config ── bool(int) ×3, == "1" ×1
    "USE_TRITON_AWQ:VLLM_USE_TRITON_AWQ:1:0"
    "DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE:VLLM_DISABLE_COMPILE_CACHE:1:0"
    "ASSETS_CACHE_MODEL_CLEAN:VLLM_ASSETS_CACHE_MODEL_CLEAN:1:0"
    "V1_USE_OUTLINES_CACHE:VLLM_V1_USE_OUTLINES_CACHE:1:0"
    # ── Server liveness ── bool(int)
    "KEEP_ALIVE:VLLM_KEEP_ALIVE_ON_ENGINE_DEATH:1:0"
    # ── Tuning ──
    # .strip().lower() in ('1','true'). ⚠️ NOT a quality knob: exceeding the derived
    # length gives nan (RoPE) or a device-side out-of-bounds error. It only downgrades
    # a startup ValueError to a warning.
    "LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_LONG_MAX_MODEL_LEN:1:0"
    # ours, read by this image's patched FP8 kernels — not in vllm/envs.py
    "STRIX_FP8_TRITON:VLLM_STRIX_FP8_TRITON:1:0"
    # ── ROCm per-kernel toggles ── bool(int) ×2, .lower() in ("true","1") ×1
    "ROCM_FP8_PADDING:VLLM_ROCM_FP8_PADDING:1:0"
    "ROCM_MOE_PADDING:VLLM_ROCM_MOE_PADDING:1:0"
    "ROCM_CUSTOM_PAGED_ATTN:VLLM_ROCM_CUSTOM_PAGED_ATTN:1:0"
    # ── Idle behaviour ── bool(int)
    "SLEEP_WHEN_IDLE:VLLM_SLEEP_WHEN_IDLE:1:0"
    # ── Security ── bool(int)   (DO_NOT_TRACK is special-cased below: two variables)
    "INSEC_SERIAL_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_INSECURE_SERIALIZATION:1:0"
    # ── API, tool calling & parsing ── bool(int) ×3
    "RESPONSES_API_STORE:VLLM_ENABLE_RESPONSES_API_STORE:1:0"
    "TOOL_JSON_ERROR_AUTOMATIC_RETRY:VLLM_TOOL_JSON_ERROR_AUTOMATIC_RETRY:1:0"
    "GPT_OSS_HARMONY_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS_OK:VLLM_GPT_OSS_HARMONY_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTIONS:1:0"
    # ── MoE models ── bool(int) ×4
    "FUSED_MOE_GROUPED_TOPK:VLLM_USE_FUSED_MOE_GROUPED_TOPK:1:0"
    "FUSED_MOE_ACTIVATION_CHUNKING:VLLM_ENABLE_FUSED_MOE_ACTIVATION_CHUNKING:1:0"
    "MOE_DP_CHUNK:VLLM_ENABLE_MOE_DP_CHUNK:1:0"
    "SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM:VLLM_DISABLE_SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM:0:1"   # INVERTED (DISABLE_)
    # ── KV cache & attention ──
    "USE_MLA:VLLM_MLA_DISABLE:0:1"                                   # INVERTED (_DISABLE)
    "ROCM_FP8_MFMA_PAGE_ATTN:VLLM_ROCM_FP8_MFMA_PAGE_ATTN:1:0"
    "CHUNKED_LOCAL_ATTN_WITH_HYBRID_KV_CACHE_OK:VLLM_ALLOW_CHUNKED_LOCAL_ATTN_WITH_HYBRID_KV_CACHE:1:0"
    # ── Multimodal input ── bool(int)
    "MEDIA_REDIRECTS_OK:VLLM_MEDIA_URL_ALLOW_REDIRECTS:1:0"
    # ── Multi-node serving ──
    # .lower() in ("true","1") — "1" chosen for consistency with its neighbours
    "PYNCCL:VLLM_DISABLE_PYNCCL:0:1"                                 # INVERTED (DISABLE_)
    "P2P_CHECK:VLLM_SKIP_P2P_CHECK:0:1"                              # INVERTED (SKIP_)
    "RANDOMIZE_DP_DUMMY_INPUTS:VLLM_RANDOMIZE_DP_DUMMY_INPUTS:1:0"
    "RAY_COMPILED_DAG_OVERLAP_COMM:VLLM_USE_RAY_COMPILED_DAG_OVERLAP_COMM:1:0"
    "RAY_WRAPPED_PP_COMM:VLLM_USE_RAY_WRAPPED_PP_COMM:1:0"
    # ── Compilation & startup cost ── (AOT_COMPILE is tri-state, special-cased below)
    "FORCE_AOT_LOAD:VLLM_FORCE_AOT_LOAD:1:0"
    "MEGA_AOT_ARTIFACT:VLLM_USE_MEGA_AOT_ARTIFACT:1:0"
    "INDUCTOR_MAX_AUTOTUNE:VLLM_ENABLE_INDUCTOR_MAX_AUTOTUNE:1:0"
    "INDUCTOR_COORDINATE_DESCENT_TUNING:VLLM_ENABLE_INDUCTOR_COORDINATE_DESCENT_TUNING:1:0"
    "STANDALONE_COMPILE:VLLM_USE_STANDALONE_COMPILE:1:0"
    "BYTECODE_HOOK:VLLM_USE_BYTECODE_HOOK:1:0"
    # ── Logging ── (LEVEL/COLOR/STREAM are menus, special-cased below)
    "CONFIGURE_LOGGING:VLLM_CONFIGURE_LOGGING:1:0"
    "DEBUG_LOG_API_SRV_RESP:VLLM_DEBUG_LOG_API_SERVER_RESPONSE:true:false"
    "LOG_LOGO:VLLM_DISABLE_LOG_LOGO:0:1"                             # INVERTED (DISABLE_)
    # ── Tracing & diagnostics ──
    # int(), not bool(int): a level, but the file offers the on/off it is used as
    "TRACE_FUNCTION:VLLM_TRACE_FUNCTION:1:0"
    # a STRING upstream (""/"0" off · "1" on · JSON for detail); malformed = silent off
    "GC_DEBUG:VLLM_GC_DEBUG:1:0"
    "DEBUG_WORKSPACE:VLLM_DEBUG_WORKSPACE:1:0"
    "LOG_MODEL_INSPECTION:VLLM_LOG_MODEL_INSPECTION:1:0"
    "DEBUG_MFU_METRICS:VLLM_DEBUG_MFU_METRICS:1:0"
    "COMPUTE_NANS_IN_LOGITS:VLLM_COMPUTE_NANS_IN_LOGITS:1:0"
    "CUSTOM_SCOPES_FOR_PROFILING:VLLM_CUSTOM_SCOPES_FOR_PROFILING:1:0"
    # ── Development ── bool(int) ×2
    "SERVER_DEV_MODE:VLLM_SERVER_DEV_MODE:1:0"
    "USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER:VLLM_USE_V2_MODEL_RUNNER:1:0"
    # ── Experimental ── bool(int) ×1, .lower() in ("true","1") ×2
    "EXPERIMENTAL_PARSER_CONTEXT:VLLM_USE_EXPERIMENTAL_PARSER_CONTEXT:1:0"
    "ROCM_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION:VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTENTION:1:0"
    "ROCM_AITER:VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER:1:0"
)

# ── vllm_menu / vllm_pick — the settings whose answer is a MENU, not a bool ──
#
# ⭐ WHY A SEPARATE MECHANISM. A boolean has two answers and both are always
# expressible. A menu has N, and for several of these ONE MEMBER MEANS "DO NOT SET
# THE VARIABLE AT ALL" — VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT is validated by env_with_choices()
# against ["NHD","HND"], which RAISES ValueError for any other value INCLUDING the
# empty string, so `auto` cannot be spelled on the wire: it has to be an absence.
# A wire of "-" is exactly that instruction.
#
# vllm_pick <SUFFIX> <user value> <member=wire> … — prints the wire, or warns and
# fails. The user's value is case-folded and space-stripped (`Auto`, `AUTO ` are
# what people type); the WIRE is emitted verbatim, because upstream's own
# validation is case-SENSITIVE.
vllm_pick() {
    # `given` keeps the user's ORIGINAL spelling for the message — `$2` is a menu
    # member by the time the loop runs, and quoting one of those back at a user who
    # never typed it is worse than saying nothing.
    local suffix=$1 given=$2 val=$2; shift 2
    local pair menu=""
    val=${val,,}; val=${val// /}
    for pair in "$@"; do
        menu="$menu ${pair%%=*}"
        [ "${pair%%=*}" = "$val" ] && { printf '%s' "${pair#*=}"; return 0; }
    done
    serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix='$given' is not one of:$menu — leaving the setting at its default. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box."
    return 1
}

# vllm_menu <SUFFIX> <native var> <member=wire> … — the whole read/validate/export.
vllm_menu() {
    local suffix=$1 var=$2; shift 2
    local ref="DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix" val wire
    val=${!ref:-}
    # Unset/blank leaves the native variable alone, exactly as for the booleans.
    [ -n "$val" ] || return 0
    wire=$(vllm_pick "$suffix" "$val" "$@") || return 0
    [ "$wire" = "-" ] && return 0
    export "$var=$wire"
}

# ── vllm_open_registry — OBSERVE an open-registry name without OWNING it ─────
#
# 🚨 THE SAME DEFECT AS vllm_menu WITH THE OPPOSITE FIX, AND THE TWO MUST NOT BE
# UNIFIED. A menu backed by a literal list in vllm/envs.py is CLOSED — nothing can add
# to it, so an unknown value is a typo and whitelisting is right. The two names below
# are backed by ExtensionManager REGISTRIES (vllm/utils/registry.py), and vLLM
# documents registering your own: `@VIDEO_LOADER_REGISTRY.register("my_loader")` plus a
# runtime import, tied to VLLM_PLUGINS. The registry only fills INSIDE the server
# process, after plugins load, so at PRE_LAUNCH a typo and a legitimate plugin name are
# INDISTINGUISHABLE. Rejecting would break a working deployment to protect a typist;
# substituting a fallback would do the same thing silently.
# ⇒ WARN, THEN PASS THROUGH UNCHANGED. Nothing is folded, trimmed or defaulted — a
# registry key is matched exactly (`self.name2class.get(cls_name)`), so any
# normalisation we did would be a value the user did not write.
#
# ⭐ AND THAT IS WHY THESE OBSERVE RATHER THAN TRANSLATE. We do not own the value, and
# observation is pass-through under the naming rule — the `--api-prefix` precedent.
#
# 🚨 THE FAILURE IS AT REQUEST TIME, NOT AT STARTUP, AND THE WARNING MUST SAY SO
# (measured at the pin, v0.16.0). Both loads happen while a REQUEST is being parsed —
# `VIDEO_LOADER_REGISTRY.load(...)` in VideoMediaIO.__init__ (multimodal/media/video.py:44)
# and `MEDIA_CONNECTOR_REGISTRY.load(envs.VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR, ...)` in both content
# parsers (entrypoints/chat_utils.py:774, 885) — so a bad name gives a box that starts,
# binds, and reports HEALTHY, and then fails every multimodal request with
# `AssertionError: Extension class <name> not found` (registry.py:49-50). Upstream's own
# comment says only "an AssertionError will be thrown" and an earlier version of this
# warning turned that into "startup fails", which is worse than saying nothing: a user
# who watches the box come up healthy concludes the warning was noise.
#
# ⚠️ A BLANK IS NOT "THE DEFAULT" HERE, IT IS THE SAME CRASH. envs.py reads
# `os.getenv(NAME, "http")`, so "" is a VALUE: it reaches load("") and the assert fires.
# The blank has to become an absence. VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR is ALSO in the named blank
# list inside vllm_env — it is one of the natives vllm.env exposes — and the two agree;
# unsetting twice is unsetting once. VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND is NOT on that list,
# because vllm.env spells it with a DROSTE_ name, which is precisely why its guard
# belongs here beside the setting rather than in a list of surface names.
#
# vllm_open_registry <native var> <label to quote back> <plural noun> <built-in> …
vllm_open_registry() {
    local var=$1 label=$2 noun=$3; shift 3
    local val name list=''
    # `${!var+set}` asks "does it EXIST" — the same question envs.py's getenv asks,
    # and the one `-z` alone cannot tell from "exists but empty".
    if [ -n "${!var+set}" ] && [ -z "${!var}" ]; then
        unset "$var"
        return 0
    fi
    val=${!var:-}
    [ -n "$val" ] || return 0
    for name in "$@"; do
        list="${list:+$list, }$name"
        [ "$val" = "$name" ] && return 0
    done
    serve::warn "$label='$val' is not one of the $noun vLLM ships ($list). Passing it through unchanged in case a plugin registers it. If nothing does, this box will still start and report healthy, and then fail every multimodal request with 'AssertionError: Extension class $val not found'. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box."
    return 0
}

# ── the built-in members of each open registry, at the pin ───────────────────
# ⭐ READ FROM THE REGISTRATION SITES, NEVER FROM THE PROSE BESIDE THEM. Upstream's own
# comment above VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND (envs.py:757-759) lists "opencv" and
# "identity"; `identity` IS NOT REGISTERED ANYWHERE at this pin and `opencv_dynamic` and
# `molmo2` are, so the comment names one backend that does not exist and misses two that
# do. An earlier pass copied that comment into vllm.env as `{opencv*}`. The truth is the
# three `@VIDEO_LOADER_REGISTRY.register(...)` decorators at multimodal/video.py:238,
# 340, 434 and the one `@MEDIA_CONNECTOR_REGISTRY.register("http")` at
# multimodal/media/connector.py:36.
# ⚠️ ENUMERATED AT DEV TIME, NOT AT BUILD TIME — reading the registry itself would mean
# importing vLLM. `scripts/vllm-registries.py` re-derives both lists from the pinned
# source and reports drift against THESE arrays when the pin moves.
VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BUILTINS=( opencv opencv_dynamic molmo2 )
VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR_BUILTINS=( http )

# vllm_env — the environment the served process gets: DROSTE_VLLM_* translated to
# the native variables, plus the 89 NATIVE lines whose blank the file promises is a
# no-op and whose reader would otherwise take the box down. Its own function so it
# can be driven alone (source the spec, call it, print the environment) without
# building the argv.
# ⚠️ EXPORT IS REQUIRED. resolve::apply_spec runs `set +a` before PRE_LAUNCH, so a
# bare assignment here would never reach the vLLM process — it would be a silent
# no-op, which is the same defect in a different costume.
vllm_env() {
    local entry suffix rest var on off val

    # ── a blank NATIVE line has to mean what the file says: nothing ────────────
    # 🚨 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES IS SHOWN BLANK (vllm.env:220) AND UNCOMMENTING IT AS
    # PRINTED TAKES EVERY GPU AWAY. Both resolvers source the file under `set -a`, so
    # the line arrives as CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="" and reaches the server:
    # droste-envfile.sh:155 exports it, and the name is not in the `loud` list at :70,
    # so it does not even warn on the way past.
    # The ROCm RUNTIME would shrug — rocclr/device/rocm/rocdevice.cpp:390-392 only
    # filters when `ordinals[0] != '\0'` — but TORCH'S PYTHON PARSER IS STRICTER THAN
    # THE RUNTIME IT WRAPS. torch/cuda/__init__.py:736-805 `_parse_visible_devices()`
    # returns `list(range(64))` when the variable is UNSET and `[]` for "" (`_strtoul("")`
    # is -1, and a negative aborts the sequence), and :938-940 `_device_count_amdsmi()`
    # returns 0 for an empty list. vLLM reads exactly that path on ROCm
    # (vllm/utils/torch_utils.py:609-620 at v0.16.0) and never falls back, because the
    # fallback is gated on `raw_count < 0` and 0 is not negative.
    # ⇒ the blank must reach the wire as an ABSENCE — and absence IS this box's real
    # default: nothing in any image or profile.d sets CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES.
    #
    # 🚨 AND CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES WAS NEVER THE ONLY ONE — IT WAS JUST THE ONE WE HAD
    # LOOKED AT (s57). vllm.env exposes 149 NATIVE (non-DROSTE_) names, and measured at
    # the pin, 88 MORE of them are fatal on a clear. Same shape as llama's list and the
    # same ruling behind it: ⭐ ANYTHING THAT COULD TAKE DOWN THE BOX ON AN EMPTY
    # STRING, WE UNSET IF EMPTY. Both resolvers source the file under `set -a`, so a
    # user who uncomments a line and then empties it hands vLLM `NAME=""`, and vLLM's
    # readers ask "is it SET", not "is it non-empty".
    #
    # 🚨 THE SELECTION CRITERION IS THE READER'S BEHAVIOR ON "", NOT WHAT THE FILE
    # DISPLAYS. The old list held one name because one blank line had been noticed;
    # `256`, `16384`, `blake3` and `fork` all behave identically once the user clears
    # them. vllm/envs.py is a dict of 218 LAMBDAS and they are NOT uniform, so each was
    # measured by CALLING it at the pin (v0.16.0, 89a77b1) with the name unset and then
    # with it set to "". Four failure shapes, and they account for all 88:
    #     73  int("")     ⇒ ValueError: invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''
    #      3  float("")   ⇒ ValueError: could not convert string to float: ''
    #     10  env_with_choices  ⇒ its None-check is at envs.py:304-306, so "" is a
    #                            VALUE and falls to `raise ValueError` at :318-322
    #      1  json.loads("")    ⇒ JSONDecodeError (ALLREDUCE_FUSION_THRESHOLDS_MB)
    #      1  VLLM_PORT   ⇒ get_vllm_port (envs.py:402-418) gates on
    #                       `"VLLM_PORT" not in os.environ`, a PRESENCE test, so a
    #                       blank skips the `return None` and reaches int("")
    #
    # ⚠️ ONE "BOOLEAN" FAMILY SPLITS ACROSS ALL THREE OUTCOMES — which is why nothing
    # here was inferred from a name. `VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM` is
    # `bool(int(os.getenv(.., "1")))` (envs.py:1132) and THROWS; the AITER flags are
    # `os.getenv(.., "True").lower() in ("true", "1")` (envs.py:896-898) and cannot
    # throw at all — a blank there silently flips a default-True flag OFF, and a
    # default-False one is a genuine no-op. Only the throwing ones are in the FIRST
    # array below; the silent flippers are in the SECOND one, added s58.
    #
    # 🚨 "DOES IT RAISE" WAS NEVER THE STANDARD — IT WAS THE FIRST SWEEP'S INSTRUMENT
    # (s58, Jei's ruling: *"we own the rewriting of these. it's our responsibility to
    # make sure the wiring prevents bringing down the box."*). The sweep that produced
    # the 88 binned the remaining names as "differs but does not raise" and never opened
    # them, while the SAME session was guarding `IPYTHONDIR` on the finetuning box —
    # which also does not raise; it just puts the profile directory in the CWD.
    #
    # ⭐ THE RULE, AND IT IS JEI'S, IN ONE LINE:
    #        A BLANK MUST BEHAVE EXACTLY AS IF THE SETTING WERE ABSENT.
    # That is the whole thing, and it makes the test per name a single comparison —
    # run the reader with the name absent, run it with the name "", compare:
    #     identical  ⇒ NOTHING TO DO. No guard, no list entry. This covers every
    #                  `x or default` and every truthiness gate, and it is why the
    #                  list must not be padded: an entry earns its place by a MEASURED
    #                  difference, and a longer list is not a better one.
    #     different  ⇒ UNSET, so that the blank becomes the absence.
    #     …unless    ⇒ the blank is itself a MEANINGFUL intention — an unbounded string
    #                  where emptying it CANCELS a file, path or list that would
    #                  otherwise load ("no API key", "no logging config file", "no LoRA
    #                  repo list"). That is the only case where unsetting is wrong.
    # ⚠️ AN UNBOUNDED STRING WHOSE BLANK IS MERELY USELESS OR HARMFUL IS NOT THAT CASE.
    # The path roots below are unbounded strings too, and a blank there is a relative
    # path or a socket bound at the filesystem root — nobody's intention. Those unset.
    # ⭐ AND WHERE THE DEFAULT COMES FROM IS IRRELEVANT (Jei, explicitly): a literal, a
    # runtime computation, something derived from the machine or the model — all fine.
    # Do not try to name or reproduce a default in order to restore it. `unset` hands
    # the decision back to the program, which is the entire point.
    #
    # The split into two arrays is DOCUMENTATION, not two policies: one call, one
    # mechanism, and `unset` restores exactly the default the file already prints.
    #
    # ⚠️ INCLUSION DOES NOT DEPEND ON WHETHER THE CODE PATH RUNS ON THIS BOX. The TPU,
    # CPU, NVIDIA-only and MI3*-only names are all on the list. envs.py reads are lazy,
    # so we cannot say which ones a given run touches — and `unset` restores exactly
    # the default the file already documents, so guarding a name that is never read
    # costs nothing while guessing wrong costs a box that will not start.
    #
    # ⚠️ A NAMED LIST, NOT A SWEEP — droste::blank_is_unset's own comment
    # (base/resolve/droste-common.sh:85-90) is the rule and it forbids a blanket
    # policy. Every DROSTE_VLLM_* keeps its blank, because there a blank is the
    # documented N1a opt-out, and unsetting those would turn "I don't want one" into
    # "here, have one". No DROSTE_-owned name appears below; that is a standing
    # invariant, not an accident of the current contents.
    #
    # ⭐ PLACEMENT IS ORDERING, NOT LOCATION. What this call must never do is run
    # BEFORE a `${NATIVE_NAME=default}` droste default, because that would delete a
    # user's blank opt-out and let the `=` put our value back. Measured for vllm: no
    # name below is written anywhere in this spec, so running first (here) or last is
    # identical today. It runs FIRST on purpose anyway — every DROSTE_VLLM_* mapping
    # below uses a plain `export`, which overwrites unconditionally, so a droste
    # setting still wins over a cleared native line exactly as it should.
    #
    # An array rather than 89 backslash continuations, so each section can carry a
    # comment. Order is vllm.env's own line order, section by section.
    local -a _fatal_on_clear=(
        # Caches & Config
        VLLM_XGRAMMAR_CACHE_MB                          # int
        # Server liveness & timeouts
        VLLM_ENGINE_READY_TIMEOUT_S                     # int
        VLLM_HTTP_TIMEOUT_KEEP_ALIVE                    # int
        # Engine internals & throughput
        VLLM_ENABLE_V1_MULTIPROCESSING                  # bool(int("")) ⇒ throws
        VLLM_RINGBUFFER_WARNING_INTERVAL                # int
        VLLM_ROCM_SLEEP_MEM_CHUNK_SIZE                  # int
        VLLM_V1_OUTPUT_PROC_CHUNK_SIZE                  # int
        VLLM_MSGPACK_ZERO_COPY_THRESHOLD                # int
        VLLM_MQ_MAX_CHUNK_BYTES_MB                      # int
        VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD                    # menu {spawn, fork}
        VLLM_FLOAT32_MATMUL_PRECISION                   # menu {highest, high, medium}
        # Idle Behaviour & Timeouts
        VLLM_RPC_TIMEOUT                                # int
        VLLM_ENGINE_ITERATION_TIMEOUT_S                 # int
        # MoE Models
        VLLM_SHARED_EXPERTS_STREAM_TOKEN_THRESHOLD      # int
        VLLM_FUSED_MOE_CHUNK_SIZE                       # int
        VLLM_MOE_DP_CHUNK_SIZE                          # int
        # KV Cache & Attention
        Q_SCALE_CONSTANT                                # int
        K_SCALE_CONSTANT                                # int
        V_SCALE_CONSTANT                                # int
        # Multimodal Input
        VLLM_IMAGE_FETCH_TIMEOUT                        # int
        VLLM_VIDEO_FETCH_TIMEOUT                        # int
        VLLM_AUDIO_FETCH_TIMEOUT                        # int
        VLLM_MEDIA_LOADING_THREAD_COUNT                 # int
        VLLM_MAX_AUDIO_CLIP_FILESIZE_MB                 # int
        VLLM_MM_HASHER_ALGORITHM                        # menu {blake3, sha256, sha512}
        # Multi-Node Serving
        CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES                            # torch — see the block above
        LOCAL_RANK                                      # int
        VLLM_PORT                                       # presence test, then int("")
        VLLM_DP_MASTER_PORT                             # int
        VLLM_EXECUTE_MODEL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS              # int
        VLLM_DP_RANK_LOCAL                              # int (defaults to VLLM_DP_RANK)
        VLLM_DP_RANK                                    # int
        VLLM_DP_SIZE                                    # int
        VLLM_RAY_PER_WORKER_GPUS                        # float
        VLLM_USE_RAY_COMPILED_DAG_CHANNEL_TYPE          # menu {auto, nccl, shm}
        # Disaggregated prefill / KV transfer (also multi-node)
        VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT                     # int
        VLLM_NIXL_ABORT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT                 # int
        VLLM_MOONCAKE_BOOTSTRAP_PORT                    # int
        VLLM_MOONCAKE_ABORT_REQUEST_TIMEOUT             # int
        VLLM_MORIIO_QP_PER_TRANSFER                     # int
        VLLM_MORIIO_POST_BATCH_SIZE                     # int
        VLLM_MORIIO_NUM_WORKERS                         # int
        VLLM_KV_EVENTS_USE_INT_BLOCK_HASHES             # int
        # Compilation & startup cost
        VLLM_COMPILE_CACHE_SAVE_FORMAT                  # menu {binary, unpacked}
        # Logging
        VLLM_LOG_STATS_INTERVAL                         # float
        VLLM_LOG_BATCHSIZE_INTERVAL                     # float
        # CUDA / NVIDIA-only Kernels — read lazily, so guard them anyway (see above)
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER                     # int
        VLLM_BLOCKSCALE_FP8_GEMM_FLASHINFER             # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP16                    # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP8                     # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_FP4                     # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_INT4                    # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_MXFP4_MXFP8             # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_MXFP4_BF16              # int
        VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_MXFP4_MXFP8_CUTLASS     # int
        VLLM_MARLIN_INPUT_DTYPE                         # menu {int8, fp8}
        VLLM_MXFP4_USE_MARLIN                           # int
        VLLM_FLASHINFER_MOE_BACKEND                     # menu {throughput, latency, …}
        VLLM_FLASHINFER_ALLREDUCE_FUSION_THRESHOLDS_MB  # json.loads("") ⇒ throws
        VLLM_FLASHINFER_WORKSPACE_BUFFER_SIZE           # int
        VLLM_HAS_FLASHINFER_CUBIN                       # int
        VLLM_ALLREDUCE_USE_SYMM_MEM                     # int
        VLLM_NVFP4_GEMM_BACKEND                         # menu {…, cutlass, marlin}
        VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM                              # bool(int("")) ⇒ throws
        VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM                          # bool(int("")) ⇒ throws
        VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM_E8M0                         # int
        VLLM_USE_DEEP_GEMM_TMA_ALIGNED_SCALES           # int
        VLLM_USE_FBGEMM                                 # int
        VLLM_DEEP_GEMM_WARMUP                           # menu {skip, full, relax}
        VLLM_DEEPEPLL_NVFP4_DISPATCH                    # int
        VLLM_DEEPEP_BUFFER_SIZE_MB                      # int
        VLLM_DEEPEP_LOW_LATENCY_USE_MNNVL               # int
        VLLM_DEEPEP_HIGH_THROUGHPUT_FORCE_INTRA_NODE    # int
        VLLM_ENABLE_CUDAGRAPH_GC                        # int
        VLLM_USE_NVFP4_CT_EMULATIONS                    # int
        VLLM_MAX_TOKENS_PER_EXPERT_FP4_MOE              # int
        VLLM_NVTX_SCOPES_FOR_PROFILING                  # int
        VLLM_DBO_COMM_SMS                               # int
        VLLM_LORA_DISABLE_PDL                           # int
        VLLM_USE_NCCL_SYMM_MEM                          # int
        # TPU / XLA (requires torch_xla & TPU)
        VLLM_XLA_CHECK_RECOMPILATION                    # int
        VLLM_XLA_USE_SPMD                               # int
        VLLM_TPU_BUCKET_PADDING_GAP                     # int
        VLLM_TPU_MOST_MODEL_LEN                         # int
        # CPU backend (this build is GPU-specific)
        VLLM_CPU_KVCACHE_SPACE                          # int
        VLLM_CPU_NUM_OF_RESERVED_CPU                    # int
        VLLM_CPU_SGL_KERNEL                             # int
        # Other AMD cards — upstream says MI3*
        VLLM_ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_QUANTIZATION             # menu {FP, INT8, …, NONE}
        VLLM_ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_MAX_SIZE_BYTES_MB        # int
    )

    # ── category 1 + 2 among the blanks that do NOT raise (s58) ───────────────
    # 🚨 EVERY NAME BELOW WAS MEASURED, NOT REASONED ABOUT. vllm/envs.py loads
    # standalone, so each of the 149 native names vllm.env exposes was read TWICE in
    # isolated interpreters at the pin (v0.16.0) — once with the name absent, once with
    # it "" — and the results diffed. 130 differ. 89 of those are the raising ones
    # above. 41 differ WITHOUT raising: 29 are category 1 or 2 and are listed here; the
    # other 12 are category 3 and are named in the block after this array.
    # ⚠️ The reader must be REGISTERED IN sys.modules before it is called: the
    # VLLM_DP_RANK_LOCAL lambda (envs.py:1044) reaches through `sys.modules[__name__]`,
    # and an unregistered module turns that into a KeyError that reads as a real
    # difference. An earlier sweep had exactly that false positive.
    #
    # ⭐ FOUR SHAPES, and naming them is what keeps the next reader from re-deriving:
    #   a default-True flag read as `.lower() in ("true","1")` ⇒ "" IS FALSE
    #   a documented default STRING replaced by "" that no consumer can use
    #   a path root joined with os.path.join/Path ⇒ RELATIVE, or Path("") == "."
    #   an `is not None` / registry gate ⇒ "" is a VALUE, so the mechanism switches ON
    local -a _wrong_on_clear=(
        # ── ten default-True ROCm flags: a blank turns hardware features OFF ──
        # envs.py:896-911, all `os.getenv(.., "True").lower() in ("true","1")`. Clearing
        # a line is not "turn this off" — it is "I have no opinion" — and this is the
        # direction that reads as a hardware fault rather than a config mistake.
        # ⚠️ ALL TEN ARE INERT ON gfx1151 TODAY and that is NOT why they are here. The
        # AITER entry points are wrapped in @if_aiter_supported, whose gate is
        # `is_on_gfx9()` = {gfx90a, gfx942, gfx950} (_aiter_ops.py:36-71, 878-881);
        # SKINNY_GEMM's three uses are `and on_gfx9()` / `on_gfx950()` / `on_mi3xx()`
        # (layers/utils.py:171-190, scaled_mm/rocm.py:83-88); QUICK_REDUCE only runs
        # inside the multi-GPU quick all-reduce. Inert-here is a reason the fix matters
        # LESS, never a reason to leave a knob lying about behaving wrongly — and the
        # existing list already guards TPU, CPU and NVIDIA-only names on that basis.
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_LINEAR
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MOE
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_RMSNORM
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MLA
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_MHA
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FP8BMM
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FP4BMM
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_TRITON_GEMM
        VLLM_ROCM_USE_SKINNY_GEMM
        VLLM_ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_CAST_BF16_TO_FP16
        # ── path roots: "" is not "the default", it is a RELATIVE path ──
        # 🚨 RPC_BASE_PATH IS THE BOX-BREAKER OF THIS GROUP. network_utils.py:141-143 is
        # `f"ipc://{base_rpc_path}/{uuid4()}"`, so "" makes the frontend↔engine ZMQ
        # socket `ipc:///<uuid>` — a unix socket at the FILESYSTEM ROOT, which the box
        # user cannot create. It is on the DEFAULT serving path, not an exotic one:
        # v1/engine/utils.py:892 takes it whenever `handshake_local_only`, which is
        # true for a single-node single-engine serve (v1/utils.py:143-156).
        VLLM_RPC_BASE_PATH                              # /tmp -> '' ⇒ ipc:///<uuid>
        # CACHE_ROOT is also the SOURCE OF A BIND: the CACHES row above persists
        # ~/.cache/vllm, so clearing it silently un-persists the compile cache as well
        # as making every join relative (compilation/backends.py:897, caching.py:399,
        # models/registry.py:693 `Path(envs.VLLM_CACHE_ROOT) / "modelinfos"`).
        VLLM_CACHE_ROOT
        VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT                                # usage_lib.py:30-32, join('',…)
        # ⭐ THE IPYTHONDIR SHAPE, EXACTLY. assets/base.py:15 is `Path(envs.…)` and
        # `Path("")` is `PosixPath('.')` (measured), so downloaded assets land in the
        # server's CWD instead of the cache.
        VLLM_ASSETS_CACHE
        VLLM_XLA_CACHE_PATH                             # same shape; TPU-only consumer
        # `is not None` at lora/ops/triton_ops/utils.py:157 and fused_moe.py:1059, so ""
        # ENTERS: a `/<gpu>_<OP>.json` probe plus a warning per LoRA op, and a
        # CWD-relative MoE config tried ahead of the shipped one.
        VLLM_TUNED_CONFIG_FOLDER
        # ── gates that read "" as a VALUE, so the mechanism switches on and misfires ──
        # 'http' -> '' ⇒ ExtensionManager.load('') asserts (utils/registry.py:49-50).
        # The server comes UP and every multimodal request fails — the NBFORMAT_VALIDATOR
        # shape, and the reason "does it raise at startup" is the wrong question.
        VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR
        # ⛔ VLLM_PLUGINS IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* ON THIS LIST — Jei ruled it s57, and the
        # mechanics are the reason it looked like it belonged. `None -> ['']` means
        # `plugin.name in ['']` is false for every plugin, so a cleared line loads NO
        # plugins where an absent one loads ALL (plugins/__init__.py:31,54). That reads
        # as the classic blank-is-not-absent defect — but here the divergence IS the
        # feature: "load no plugins" is a thing a user may legitimately want to say, and
        # an empty list is the only way to say it. It is the unbounded-string exception,
        # and `vllm.env` documents the behaviour at the line. ⭐ The near-identical
        # mechanism next door (MEDIA_CONNECTOR) IS guarded, because "no media connector"
        # is not a coherent request — the difference is intent, not machinery.
        # `if partition_list_str is not None` (distributed/utils.py:110-116) ⇒ ""
        # enters and `int('')` raises "Invalid partition string: ".
        VLLM_PP_LAYER_PARTITION
        # SharedMemory(name="", create=True) ⇒ OSError [Errno 22] '/'  (measured here).
        VLLM_OBJECT_STORAGE_SHM_BUFFER_NAME
        # 'strict' -> '' ⇒ not in ("strict","fill","span") ⇒ ValueError
        # (v1/engine/utils.py:397-404).
        VLLM_RAY_DP_PACK_STRATEGY
        # ── a printed default replaced by a value nothing can use ──
        VLLM_CPU_OMP_THREADS_BIND                       # 'auto' -> '' ⇒ autobind never runs
        VLLM_DP_MASTER_IP                               # '127.0.0.1' -> ''
        VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_HOST                     # 'localhost' -> ''
        VLLM_USAGE_STATS_SERVER                         # the URL -> ''
        VLLM_USAGE_SOURCE                               # 'production' -> ''
        VLLM_PROCESS_NAME_PREFIX                        # 'VLLM' -> '' ⇒ titles read "::x"
        VLLM_TEST_FORCE_LOAD_FORMAT                     # 'dummy' -> ''
        # `assert so_file is not None` PASSES on "" and ctypes.CDLL("") then SUCCEEDS
        # (measured), so a clear turns a legible AssertionError with the fix in it
        # (cuda_wrapper.py:115-119) into a handle carrying no cudart symbols.
        VLLM_CUDART_SO_PATH
    )

    # ── class 2 proper: a name that is not vLLM's at all (s58) ────────────────
    # 🚨 THE MEASURED DIFFERENCE IS NOT IN A vLLM READER — IT IS IN A LOADER THAT
    # COPIES THE VALUE ONWARD. model_loader/runai_streamer_loader.py:53-57 is
    #     aws_endpoint_url = os.getenv("AWS_ENDPOINT_URL")
    #     if runai_streamer_s3_endpoint is None and aws_endpoint_url is not None:
    #         os.environ["RUNAI_STREAMER_S3_ENDPOINT"] = aws_endpoint_url
    # an `is not None` gate, so a cleared line hands the Run:ai streamer an EMPTY
    # endpoint where an absent one leaves the streamer to resolve its own. Measured in
    # two interpreters: absent leaves RUNAI_STREAMER_S3_ENDPOINT unset, "" sets it to
    # "". Exactly the shape the array above is full of, one package further out.
    # ⚠️ THE TWO CREDENTIAL NAMES ARE NOT HERE, and that is a measurement too — see the
    # not-guarded list below. A longer list is not a better one.
    # ⚠️ AND IT IS ITS OWN ARRAY BECAUSE IT IS NOT A KEY IN vllm/envs.py. The suite
    # cross-checks every guarded name against upstream's env dict, which is what would
    # catch a name renamed out from under the pin — and that check only means something
    # if the names it walks really are vLLM's. This one is botocore's and tensorizer's.
    local -a _class2_on_clear=(
        AWS_ENDPOINT_URL                                # runai_streamer_loader.py:53-57
    )

    # ⭐ AND THE ELEVEN THAT ARE DELIBERATELY NOT GUARDED, NAMED SO THAT "not on the
    # list" is a decision rather than an omission. For the nine vLLM natives TWO
    # INDEPENDENT REASONS AGREE, which is the strongest evidence either is right:
    #   · a blank ALREADY BEHAVES AS AN ABSENCE. envs.py hands back "" where it would
    #     hand back None, but every consumer gates on TRUTHINESS, so the difference
    #     never reaches a decision — `if not model_redirect_path: return model`
    #     (transformers_utils/utils.py:80-83), `if so_file:` (utils/nccl.py:22-26),
    #     `if lora_cache_dir:` (lora_resolvers/filesystem_resolver.py:52-53),
    #     `[key for key in (args.api_key or [envs.VLLM_API_KEY]) if key]`
    #     (openai/api_server.py:240), `if not log_config_file:`
    #     (openai/server_utils.py:112). Nothing to fix ⇒ nothing to list.
    #   · and each is an UNBOUNDED string naming a credential, a file or a list to
    #     load, so a blank is the user saying "none" — a real capability, not a
    #     mistake. Guarding one would be the single way this rule can go wrong.
    #   VLLM_API_KEY   VLLM_LOGGING_CONFIG_PATH   VLLM_MODEL_REDIRECT_PATH
    #   VLLM_LORA_RESOLVER_CACHE_DIR   VLLM_LORA_RESOLVER_HF_REPO_LIST
    #   VLLM_NCCL_SO_PATH   VLLM_NCCL_INCLUDE_PATH   CUDA_HOME
    #   VLLM_DISABLED_KERNELS
    # ⚠️ THE OTHER TWO SIT HERE ON ONE REASON, NOT TWO, AND THE SECOND DOES NOT APPLY.
    # AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID and AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY are class 2 — botocore owns the
    # contract — and a blank credential is not the user saying "none", it is the user
    # saying nothing: EnvProvider.load() gates on `if access_key:` (botocore
    # credentials.py), so "" makes the environment provider decline and the chain moves
    # on to ~/.aws and the instance metadata exactly as an absence does. MEASURED at
    # botocore 1.43.83 with HOME pointed at an empty directory: absent and "" both give
    # `Session().get_credentials() -> None`, and a real pair still resolves. Nothing to
    # fix, so nothing to list.
    #   AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID   AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY
    # 🚨 S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID / S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / S3_ENDPOINT_URL ARE OFF THIS LIST
    # BECAUSE THEY ARE OFF THE SURFACE, NOT BECAUSE THE VERDICT CHANGED — AND THE REASON
    # RECORDED FOR THEM WAS WRONG. They were filed under "a blank already behaves as an
    # absence… every consumer gates on truthiness", and there is no consumer at all:
    # envs.py:621-623 reads all three, tensorizer.py:372-378 resolves them into
    # self.s3_*, then :380-384 builds stream_kwargs from tensorizer_config.* instead,
    # and no module reads a self.s3_* field ever again (grepped across the pinned tree,
    # identical on upstream main). Note that the citations above name a gate site for
    # each of the nine and named none for these three — because none existed.
    # ⭐ A DEAD NAME CANNOT BEHAVE CORRECTLY; IT CAN ONLY LOOK AS THOUGH IT DOES.
    # vllm.env exposes botocore's names in their place, which every S3 path in this
    # image really reads. ⚠️ AND A NAME THIS LIST KEEPS AFTER vllm.env DROPS IT IS
    # UNAUDITABLE — the suite's phantom check is what holds the two in step.
    # ⚠️ VLLM_CUDART_SO_PATH IS THE NEAR MISS AND IS IN THE ARRAY ABOVE, NOT HERE. It
    # looks like a sibling of VLLM_NCCL_SO_PATH — same shape, same kind of value — but
    # its consumer is `assert so_file is not None` and then `ctypes.CDLL(so_file)`, and
    # CDLL("") SUCCEEDS (measured). So a blank does not behave as an absence there, and
    # it does not mean "none" either: it means a library handle with no cudart symbols.
    # ⭐ THE 19 NAMES WHOSE ACCESSOR ITSELF RETURNS THE SAME THING EITHER WAY are not
    # listed at all, here or above — VLLM_HOST_IP, VLLM_LOOPBACK_IP, the default-False
    # AITER flags, and so on. There is nothing to decide about them.
    droste::blank_is_unset "${_fatal_on_clear[@]}" "${_wrong_on_clear[@]}" \
                           "${_class2_on_clear[@]}"

    # ── the two XDG bases vllm.env QUOTES but does not EXPOSE (s58) ───────────
    # 🚨 FOUR OF THE FILE'S LINES DOCUMENT THEIR DEFAULT AS `${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/
    # vllm…` — vllm.env:75-77 (VLLM_ASSETS_CACHE, VLLM_CACHE_ROOT, VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT) and
    # :418 (VLLM_XLA_CACHE_PATH); THREE cache lines and ONE config line, not four of the
    # former. Those four sentences are TRUE for an absent base and FALSE for a blank one.
    # envs.py:236-247 resolves both bases with `os.getenv(NAME, <default>)`, an
    # ABSENT-ONLY default, and every route into this box's environment delivers a
    # cleared line as "" (both resolvers source the file under `set -a`). MEASURED at the
    # pin by loading vllm/envs.py in isolated interpreters with HOME=/home/boxuser:
    #                          absent                    ""
    #   VLLM_CACHE_ROOT        ~/.cache/vllm             vllm
    #   VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT       ~/.config/vllm            vllm
    #   VLLM_ASSETS_CACHE      ~/.cache/vllm/assets      vllm/assets
    #   VLLM_XLA_CACHE_PATH    ~/.cache/vllm/xla_cache   vllm/xla_cache
    # ⇒ RELATIVE paths, resolved against the server's CWD instead of behind a bind. The
    # box starts, serves and reports itself healthy while its caches land inside the
    # container and vanish at the next recreate — the loud_dirs symptom
    # (droste-envfile.sh:114), except that here the user asked for the DEFAULT.
    # ⭐ SO THE FIX IS OURS AND IT IS HERE, NOT IN THE FILE. The four lines are accurate
    # prose about the option; making a blank behave as the absence makes them accurate in
    # every case, and touches nothing the user authored.
    # ⚠️ AND `${XDG_CACHE_HOME-~/.cache}` IS NOT THE SAME FIX — a shell with an empty base
    # yields `/vllm` where python yields `vllm`. That is a third wrong answer, not a
    # cheaper right one.
    # ⚠️ THE FOUR NATIVES ARE ALREADY IN _wrong_on_clear ABOVE AND IT DOES NOT HELP HERE:
    # in this scenario not one of them is set, so that list has no blank to see. vLLM
    # computes the bad path itself, from a blank INPUT one layer further out.
    # ⚠️ NOT IN A NAMED LIST, AND IT MUST NOT BE ADDED TO ONE. Those arrays are the
    # natives vllm.env EXPOSES; XDG_CACHE_HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME are settings on
    # nobody's surface — they appear only inside the `${…}` of the four lines above — so
    # listing them would make the suite's phantom check ("every guarded name is exposed
    # by vllm.env") and its envs.py key cross-check (neither name is a key) false, and a
    # check with an exemption in it stops holding the list honest. The guard belongs
    # beside the consumers, exactly as for VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT above.
    # ⭐ EACH NAME EARNS ITS OWN PLACE. XDG_CONFIG_HOME has exactly one consumer in this
    # image (VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT) and it differs, measured — it is guarded on that evidence,
    # not for family symmetry with the cache line. Nothing else in the XDG family is
    # touched: droste sets none of them and the rest have no measured consequence here.
    # ⭐ AND THIS COVERS ROUTES droste-envfile.sh CANNOT SEE — a create-time `--env`, or an
    # `export XDG_CACHE_HOME=` typed inside `distrobox enter` — because it reads the
    # environment the server is about to get rather than the file.
    # ⚠️ SILENT, like every other blank guard: the blank IS the request for the default,
    # and delivering it is not ignoring the user. When the value did come from the box's
    # file, load_env_file has already said the line was seen (XDG_CACHE_HOME is in its
    # loud_dirs) — though its sentence describes a MOVED directory, so for a CLEARED one
    # it warns about a hazard this guard has just removed. Worth fixing there, not here.
    if [ -n "${XDG_CACHE_HOME+set}" ] && [ -z "$XDG_CACHE_HOME" ]; then
        unset XDG_CACHE_HOME
    fi
    if [ -n "${XDG_CONFIG_HOME+set}" ] && [ -z "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME" ]; then
        unset XDG_CONFIG_HOME
    fi

    # ── the booleans ──
    for entry in "${VLLM_BOOL_VARS[@]}"; do
        suffix=${entry%%:*}; rest=${entry#*:}
        var=${rest%%:*};     rest=${rest#*:}
        on=${rest%%:*};      off=${rest#*:}
        val="DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix"; val=${!val:-}
        # Unset/blank leaves the variable alone: the image's baked value or vLLM's
        # own default stands. Setting it here would turn an opt-out into an opt-in.
        [ -n "$val" ] || continue
        # droste::bool normalises BOTH user vocabularies to one internal answer, so
        # there are two arms here and not four. yes/no and on/off are not synonyms
        # in the FILE — one answers a question ("never reach the network?"), the
        # other names a state ("padding is on") — and each setting is worded as
        # whichever it actually is. That distinction is the user's to read; by the
        # time a value reaches here it has been resolved and the wording is spent.
        case "$(droste::bool "$val")" in
            on)  export "$var=$on" ;;
            off) export "$var=$off" ;;
            *) serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_$suffix='$val' is not a yes/no or on/off value — leaving $var as it is. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box." ;;
        esac
    done

    # ── the menus ──
    #
    # 🚨 KV_CACHE_LAYOUT AND VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND ARE THE SAME DEFECT WITH OPPOSITE
    # FIXES — DO NOT UNIFY THEM. The layout is a CLOSED ENUM: the valid names are a
    # literal list in vllm/envs.py, nothing can add to it, so an unknown value is a
    # typo and the right answer is to whitelist. The video backend is an OPEN
    # REGISTRY: a plugin may register a loader under any name, so at PRE_LAUNCH time
    # a typo and a legitimate plugin name are INDISTINGUISHABLE and refusing would
    # break a working deployment. Whitelist the closed one; pass the open one
    # through with a warning. (See the VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND block below.)
    #
    # `auto` = "do not set it": env_with_choices raises for anything outside
    # NHD/HND, and that includes both `auto` and the empty string.
    #
    # 🚨 THE NATIVE NAME HAS TO GO ON WORKING, AND ITS BLANK IS FATAL. vllm.env spells
    # this setting DROSTE_VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT, but every config file is seeded
    # `if_missing` and never rewritten, so a box may carry a hand-written native
    # `VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=` line forever — and a user may add one at any time, because
    # every native VLLM_* name is reachable through this file by design. Both resolvers
    # source it under `set -a`, so an emptied line arrives as `VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=""`,
    # and env_with_choices (envs.py:303-325) returns its default ONLY for `None`: "" is a
    # VALUE, misses ["NHD","HND"] and raises ValueError before the server binds. The box
    # then restart-loops with nothing in the log a user can act on.
    # ⚠️ IT IS NOT IN THE NAMED BLANK LIST ABOVE and must not be added there — that list
    # is the natives vllm.env EXPOSES, and a phantom entry would make it unauditable.
    # The guard belongs beside the setting, exactly as for the two open registries.
    if [ -n "${VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT+set}" ] && [ -z "$VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT" ]; then
        unset VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT
    fi
    #
    # ⭐ PRECEDENCE, STATED ONCE SO IT IS NOT RE-DERIVED: the droste setting wins ONLY
    # when it names a layout. `auto` — the value vllm.env SHIPS — leaves the native
    # variable exactly as it found it, and so do absent, blank and a rejected value.
    # That is not laziness: `auto` is the printed default, so uncommenting the line as
    # shown must be a no-op, and deleting a native line the user wrote elsewhere in the
    # same file is the opposite of a no-op. A user who wants the backend to choose
    # removes their own native line; a user who writes NHD in either spelling gets NHD.
    vllm_menu KV_CACHE_LAYOUT VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT auto=- nhd=NHD hnd=HND

    # `auto` here is upstream's own COMPUTED default (torch version + whether the
    # compile cache is disabled), so it likewise has to be an absence — there is no
    # literal that means "work it out yourself".
    vllm_menu AOT_COMPILE VLLM_USE_AOT_COMPILE auto=- on=1 off=0

    # ⚠️ `notset` IS NOT "unset". Python resolves NOTSET on a handler by walking up
    # to the root logger's effective level, which lands on WARNING — QUIETER than
    # leaving the variable alone (unset ⇒ vLLM's own "INFO"). Two "unsets" one layer
    # apart, and the file offers the one that surprises people. Upstream .upper()s
    # the value, so the wire is the canonical spelling.
    vllm_menu LOGGING_LEVEL VLLM_LOGGING_LEVEL \
        debug=DEBUG info=INFO warning=WARNING warn=WARN \
        error=ERROR critical=CRITICAL fatal=FATAL notset=NOTSET

    # ⚠️ THE NATIVE VARIABLE IS NOT A WORD, IT IS A DIGIT. logger.py:30-38 tests
    # `== "0"` then `== "1"` and treats EVERYTHING ELSE as auto — so `always` and
    # `never`, the words a person would reach for, both silently mean auto. That is
    # the whole reason this one is droste-named. `auto` is wired to the literal
    # upstream default rather than to "-" because writing it is faithful: it names
    # the isatty branch that upstream itself falls through to.
    # (NO_COLOR is honoured by upstream ahead of all three; we do not touch it.)
    vllm_menu LOGGING_COLOR VLLM_LOGGING_COLOR auto=auto always=1 never=0

    # ⚠️ The native value is a logging-dictConfig `ext://` REFERENCE, not a word.
    # A value that resolves to a non-stream object configures CLEANLY and then
    # AttributeErrors on every single log record; only an unresolvable ext:// fails
    # at startup. So the menu is closed and short on purpose.
    vllm_menu LOGGING_STREAM VLLM_LOGGING_STREAM \
        stdout=ext://sys.stdout stderr=ext://sys.stderr

    # ── the settings that are not a bool and not a menu ──

    # 🚨 ONE ANSWER, TWO VARIABLES — AND THE "OFF" WIRE IS AN ABSENCE.
    # vLLM reads `VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK or DO_NOT_TRACK or "0"` and compares to "1"
    # (envs.py:629-634). Python's `or` SELECTS the first non-EMPTY operand, so
    # writing VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK=0 would MASK a bare DO_NOT_TRACK=1 the user set for
    # every tool on the machine — a privacy setting silently reversed by us. So
    # `no` UNSETS ours and lets the generic one through, and only VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS
    # (which has no such chain, and which the IMAGE bakes to 1) is written to 0.
    # ⚠️ There is a third opt-out we do not manage: a file at
    # $VLLM_CONFIG_ROOT/do_not_track. This image does not persist ~/.config/vllm.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK:-}
    if [ -n "$val" ]; then
        case "$(droste::bool "$val")" in
            on)  export VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK=1 VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=1 ;;
            off) unset VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK; export VLLM_NO_USAGE_STATS=0 ;;
            *) serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_DO_NOT_TRACK='$val' is not a yes/no value — leaving telemetry as the image set it (opted out). Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box." ;;
        esac
    fi

    # ── the two OPEN REGISTRIES (see vllm_open_registry above) ────────────────
    #
    # ⚠️ THE WARNING IS ON THE VALUE THAT REACHES vLLM, NOT ON THE NAME THE USER TYPED.
    # The translation runs FIRST and the observation SECOND, so whichever spelling the
    # value arrived under, exactly one line is printed and it describes what the server
    # will actually be handed. Checking the DROSTE_ name alone left a native
    # `VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND=` line — legal in this file, and the only spelling for
    # anyone following upstream's documentation — passing unobserved and unwarned.
    # ⭐ The label follows the same principle: quote back the name the user wrote.
    local label=VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND:-}
    if [ -n "$val" ]; then
        export VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND="$val"
        label=DROSTE_VLLM_VIDEO_LOAD_BACKEND
    fi
    vllm_open_registry VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BACKEND "$label" \
        "video loaders" "${VLLM_VIDEO_LOADER_BUILTINS[@]}"

    # ⭐ A GENUINE MENU OF ONE, AND IT IS STILL WORTH OBSERVING. `http` is the only
    # connector vLLM registers at this pin, so ANY other value is either a plugin or a
    # typo — the same two possibilities as the video loader, with the same rule. It is
    # NATIVE-named on the surface (vllm.env:212) because we observe it without owning
    # it; do not give it a DROSTE_ name to "fix" the fatality, because the open registry
    # is the reason a whitelist cannot be the answer here.
    vllm_open_registry VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR \
        "media connectors" "${VLLM_MEDIA_CONNECTOR_BUILTINS[@]}"

    # A PATH, not a switch — vllm.env:320 shows it BLANK and offers no menu, so the
    # value goes through verbatim and blank is the off-state.
    # 🚨 AND THE OFF-STATE HAS TO BE AN ABSENCE, NOT AN EMPTY STRING. envs.py:573
    # reads `os.environ.get("VLLM_DEBUG_DUMP_PATH", None)` and the default is
    # `str | None = None` (envs.py:218), so a blank is NOT None and every
    # `is not None` gate downstream fires on it. Exporting the blank the file shows
    # would switch the mechanism on and dump to "" — which is why the guard below is
    # load-bearing rather than tidiness.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_DEBUG_DUMP_PATH:-}
    [ -n "$val" ] && export VLLM_DEBUG_DUMP_PATH="$val"

    # ⚠️ int(), so a non-numeric value is a ValueError at import — before any log
    # line the user could read. Digits only, and we refuse rather than guess.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_TOOL_PARSE_REGEX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS:-}
    if [ -n "$val" ]; then
        case "$val" in
            ''|*[!0-9]*) serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_TOOL_PARSE_REGEX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS='$val' is not a whole number of seconds — leaving it at vLLM's default of 1. Fix it in $ENV_FILE and restart the box." ;;
            *) export VLLM_TOOL_PARSE_REGEX_TIMEOUT_SECONDS="$val" ;;
        esac
    fi

    # ⭐ AN "ADD TO", NOT A "REPLACE" (vllm.env:221). The native LD_LIBRARY_PATH used to
    # be on the config surface, shown blank — a default the box does not deliver, since
    # base/Container.runtime:125 bakes /opt/rocm/lib:/opt/rocm/lib64 — and its semantics
    # are REPLACE, so uncommenting it as printed threw the ROCm library paths away. The
    # setting is now additive, and the addition goes AFTER the baked value: a user
    # directory searched first could shadow a ROCm library, and that reads as a hardware
    # fault rather than as a config mistake. Blank (the shipped default) does nothing.
    droste::ld_library_path_add "${DROSTE_VLLM_LD_LIBRARY_PATH_ADD:-}"

    # 🚨 THE VALUE IS THE NAME OF AN fx GRAPH NODE, AND THE GATE IS `is not None`.
    # pass_manager.py:61-63 forwards whatever it finds to torch's
    # TORCHINDUCTOR_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG, and torch compares it `== node.name`
    # (_inductor/pattern_matcher.py:1979). envs.py:573-574 reads
    # `os.environ.get("VLLM_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG", None)` against a `str | None = None`
    # default (envs.py:217), so an EMPTY value is NOT None: it switches the mechanism
    # on and then matches no node. **The blank vllm.env:321 shows must reach the wire
    # as an ABSENCE**, which is exactly what the `-n` guard does.
    # ⭐ A PLAIN VALUE SETTING, NOT A BOOLEAN (vllm.env, s56 — Jei moved this line and
    # DEBUG_DUMP_PATH OUT of the `{on, off*}` block above them). It therefore has no
    # menu, takes no on/off, and MUST NOT warn about one: `on` is simply a node name
    # that nothing will match, and second-guessing the user's node name is not ours to
    # do. The earlier bool-parsing version refused `on` and read `off` as "unset" —
    # both are gone with the menu that justified them.
    val=${DROSTE_VLLM_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG:-}
    [ -n "$val" ] && export VLLM_PATTERN_MATCH_DEBUG="$val"
    # ⚠️ `[ -n … ] && …` returns non-zero on a blank, and this is the LAST command in
    # the function — under `set -e` in both lanes that would fail PRE_LAUNCH for every
    # box that never set the variable, i.e. all of them. Return success explicitly.
    return 0
}

# ── the config must yield at least one key, or vLLM dies before it starts ────
# 🚨 THE FAILURE THIS PREVENTS IS A TRACEBACK, NOT A BAD SETTING.
# vllm/utils/argparse_utils.py:484 is `config = yaml.safe_load(config_file)` and
# :492 is `for key, value in config.items():` with NO None guard between them. A
# config whose keys are ALL commented out loads as None, so `.items()` raises
# AttributeError before the server binds, logs a line of its own, or reports
# anything a user could act on.
# ⭐ WHICH IS WHY vllm_config.yaml KEEPS ONE DELIBERATELY INERT KEY ACTIVE, under a
# "Do NOT comment out this line or remove it!" note. `enable-layerwise-nvtx-tracing`
# was chosen precisely BECAUSE it does nothing here: :493-495 emits no argument at
# all for a false bool, so the anchor cannot collide with any real configuration.
# That is the right choice of key — and it is still a kludge, because it defends by
# asking a user to heed a comment. This guard is the part that does not.
#
# ⭐ ASK THE QUESTION THE READER ASKS. "Is there a line that is not a comment" is a
# heuristic that can disagree with the parser over quoting, indentation or a
# document marker. safe_load IS the authority on what vLLM will see, so the test
# runs the same loader.
#
# 🚨 AND ONLY ONE OF THE FAILING SHAPES IS REPAIRABLE — appending to the other two
# makes them WORSE, which is how the first version of this guard was wrong:
#   None            an all-comment file. Appending a key yields a valid mapping.
#                   ANCHORABLE, and this is the case that actually happens.
#   a dict          safe, INCLUDING an empty one: `{}.items()` iterates zero times,
#                   so vLLM starts with no config-supplied arguments. Not our
#                   business to second-guess.
#   list / scalar   `.items()` fails just as it does on None, but appending a
#                   mapping key to a list document is a SYNTAX ERROR — measured.
#                   The "repair" would trade a reported failure for a parse error,
#                   so we warn plainly and pass it through instead.
# ⚠️ A file that will not parse at all is NOT our failure to pre-empt either: vLLM
# reports it at :485-489 WITH THE PATH, which is more useful than anything we could
# say. We stay quiet and let it through.
#
# ⚠️ THE USER'S FILE IS NEVER REWRITTEN. The anchor goes into a COPY, in the program
# cache's state dir (which resets every container start, so it cannot go stale), and
# --config is pointed at the copy. Editing a file the user authored, to fix a
# condition the user created, would hide the very thing the warning is announcing.
: "${VLLM_CONFIG_ANCHOR:=enable-layerwise-nvtx-tracing: false}"
vllm_config_guard() {
    local src=${1:-} derived shape
    [ -n "$src" ] && [ -r "$src" ] || return 0
    command -v python3 >/dev/null 2>&1 || return 0

    # ok | empty | notmap | unreadable — a WORD, not an exit status, so a future
    # shape can be added without renumbering anything.
    shape=$(python3 -c '
import sys, yaml
try:
    with open(sys.argv[1]) as fh:
        cfg = yaml.safe_load(fh)
except Exception:
    print("unreadable"); raise SystemExit(0)
if cfg is None:
    print("empty")
elif isinstance(cfg, dict):
    print("ok")
else:
    print("notmap")
' "$src" 2>/dev/null) || shape=unreadable

    case "$shape" in
        ok|unreadable|"") return 0 ;;
        notmap)
            serve::warn "$src does not describe a set of settings — it parses as a list or a bare value, not as 'key: value' pairs. vLLM will abort while loading it. Droste cannot repair this shape (adding a key to it would make the file unparseable), so it is being passed through unchanged for vLLM to report. Fix the top-level structure of $src and restart the box."
            return 0 ;;
    esac

    derived=${DROSTE_SERVE_STATE_DIR:-/tmp}/vllm_config.anchored.yaml
    mkdir -p "$(dirname "$derived")" 2>/dev/null || true
    if ! cp -- "$src" "$derived" 2>/dev/null ||
       ! printf '\n# Added by droste — see the warning in the container log.\n%s\n' \
            "$VLLM_CONFIG_ANCHOR" >>"$derived" 2>/dev/null; then
        serve::warn "$src DEFINES NO SETTINGS and the anchored copy could not be written to $derived — vLLM is about to fail on AttributeError while loading it. Uncomment a setting in $src, or restore its '$VLLM_CONFIG_ANCHOR' anchor line."
        return 0
    fi

    # ⚠️ WORDING IS DELIBERATELY BROADER THAN "every line is commented out". That is
    # the case that actually happens, but the test is "does it load as a NON-EMPTY
    # MAPPING", which a list-shaped or scalar file also fails — and a message that
    # named the wrong cause would send someone hunting for a comment marker that is
    # not there.
    serve::warn "$src DEFINES NO SETTINGS — it does not load as a mapping of keys, which is what happens when every line is commented out. vLLM cannot use such a file: it aborts before startup instead of reporting the problem. Droste is serving an anchored COPY ($derived) with '$VLLM_CONFIG_ANCHOR' appended so this box can still start. YOUR FILE WAS NOT MODIFIED. Restore that anchor line in $src, or uncomment a real setting, and restart the box."
    DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG=$derived
    return 0
}

# ── PRE_LAUNCH (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVICE-rebuild (see build-spec.example): fold $DROSTE_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS into the argv —
# CLI args placed after --config override the config file's values (vLLM's own
# CLI-over-config merge), exactly as the generated config header documents.
# The model rides the config; stale-graph handling is a documented one-liner
# (compile cache is disabled), not an automated pre-launch step.
PRE_LAUNCH="vllm_pre_launch"
vllm_pre_launch() {
    # ── a DROSTE_-owned name whose blank is NOT a coherent "off" (s58) ─────────
    # 🚨 THE `:=` AT THE TOP OF THIS FILE DOES NOT COVER THE CASE THAT MATTERS. It runs
    # when the SPEC is sourced; the user's file is applied AFTER that and BEFORE this
    # hook (resolve::apply_spec steps 6 and 7, droste-resolve.sh:836-840), so a
    # `DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG=` line arrives too late for the `:=` to see and simply
    # OVERWRITES the default with "". Measured: the argv then becomes
    # `vllm serve --config ''`, and vllm/utils/argparse_utils.py:472-475 takes
    # `"".split(".")[-1]` == "" and raises `ValueError: Config file must be of a
    # yaml/yml type.  supplied` before it ever opens a file — so the box never binds,
    # never logs anything a user can act on, and restart-loops.
    # ⚠️ THE OLD HARNESS ROW FOR THIS PASSED, AND THAT IS THE LESSON. It exported the
    # blank BEFORE sourcing the spec, which is the one order production never uses, so
    # it was measuring the `:=` rather than the box. A harness that sources less than
    # production proves less than it claims.
    # ⭐ CATEGORY 1, NOT AN N1a OPT-OUT. The blank opt-out rule ("absent ⇒ ours, set ⇒
    # theirs, blank ⇒ off") only applies where "off" is a state the setting HAS. There
    # is no "serve with no config file" here — vLLM is being handed --config
    # unconditionally — so a blank cannot mean anything but "give me the default".
    # ⚠️ THIS DOES NOT TOUCH THE OPEN QUESTION ABOVE about whether a user may set this
    # at all. A non-empty value still wins, exactly as before; only the empty case
    # changes, and an empty case was never a value.
    if [ -n "${DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG+set}" ] && [ -z "$DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG" ]; then
        DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG=${VLLM_CONFIG_DEFAULT:-/opt/data/vllm_config.yaml}
        export DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG
        serve::err "DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG is set but empty in $ENV_FILE, and vLLM cannot be started without a config file — using $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG instead. Give it a path or comment the line out, and restart the box."
    fi

    vllm_env

    # Runs BEFORE SERVICE is built: the guard may repoint $DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG at an
    # anchored copy, and the argv has to carry the path we actually intend to serve.
    vllm_config_guard "$DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG"

    # Quote-aware split (droste::split_args): a value may contain spaces.
    # shellcheck disable=SC2206
    mapfile -d '' -t _extra < <(droste::split_args "${DROSTE_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS:-}")
    SERVICE=( vllm serve --config "$DROSTE_VLLM_CONFIG" ${_extra[@]+"${_extra[@]}"} )
}
